 To create a multi-column text display in Adobe JavaScript (AJDS) for a text field, you can use the `textFlow` and `Paragraph` objects. Here's a simple example of how to create a two-column layout:

```javascript
// Get the text field
var textField = app.activeDocument.textFrames.item(0);

// Create a new text flow
var textFlow = new TextFlow();

// Loop through the text in the text field
for (var i = 0; i < textField.contents.length; i++) {
    // Create a new paragraph
    var paragraph = new Paragraph();

    // Add the text to the paragraph
    paragraph.text = textField.contents.item(i);

    // Set the column properties
    paragraph.properties.justify = Justification.JUSTIFY_ALL;
    paragraph.properties.columnCount = 2;
    paragraph.properties.columnWidth = textField.width / paragraph.properties.columnCount;

    // Add the paragraph to the text flow
    textFlow.add(paragraph);
}

// Replace the text field's text with the new text flow
textField.contents = textFlow;
```

This script will divide the text in the first text frame of the active document into two columns. You can adjust the `columnWidth` property to change the width of each column.

